1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rebbe Avraml's mother became an orphan at a young age and she was raised in the home of her grandfather, the Rebbe of Lenchitz, Rebbe Zev Wolf Auerbach Z”L. She was already a grown young woman without a suitor. The
2 CONC  orphan cried her eyes out, but her grandfather gave her hope, saying that when the right time came, she will be helped.
2 CONT
2 CONT Once, a peasant-Jew came to the Lenchitzer Rebbe, to arrange for the burial of his deceased wife. After the Rebbe explained all the rites to him, he said to him: “Be so kind as to come in to me after the shiva. I have to discuss a
2 CONC n important matter with you.”
2 CONT
2 CONT When the peasant Jew came to the rebbe after the shiva, he proposed to him that he marry his granddaughter, the orphan, Rhoda. Obviously the rebbe knew the “peasant-Jew” very well, but the orphan girl was shocked – to marry a wido
2 CONC wer, of all things – someone who is much older than her, and besides, a peasant-Jew, a lessee – is this supposed to be her destined one?
2 CONT
2 CONT But the grandfather calmed her and assured her that with this widower she will have children who will light the Jewish world. It was only then that she agreed to the shiduch (marriage).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
