2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=28727&pgnum=181
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Elimelech Menachem Mendel Landau of Strikov (1859-1936). Born Menachem Mendel (Elimelech was added a year before his petira) to Rabbi Dov Berish Landau of Strikov and Biala. After the petira of Rabbi Yitzchak of Vorka in 184
2 CONC 8, the majority of Vorka Chassidim chose to follow Rabbi Menachem Mendel’s father, Rabbi Dov Berish. After his petirah in 1876, none of the sons were willing to accept leadership, so the Chassidim followed Rabbi Dov Berish’s prima
2 CONC ry talmid, Rabbi Yechiel of Alexander. Rabbi Menachem Mendel and his brothers moved to Alexander to follow Rabbi Yechiel, and – after his petirah in 1894 – his son, the Yismach Yisrael. When the Yismach Yisrael died childless in 1
2 CONC 910, Rabbbi Menachem Mendel’s brother, Rabbi Aharon Tzvi founded a court. Only when he passed, did Menachem Mendel accept leadership of the Chassidim and set up court in Strikov. After World War I, he settled in the town of Zhgier
2 CONC zh, adjacent to Lodz, and founded Yeshivas Beis Aharon, named after his brother. When he visited Eretz Yisrael, he founded Yeshivas Zechusa DeAvraham. His divrei Torah were printed in Maggid Devarav L’Yaakov and in Bayeshishim Cha
2 CONC chmah. His son, Rabbi Yaakov Yitzchak Dan, succeeded him and was murdered by the Nazis (4 Cheshvan 1943). His son, Rabbi Avraham survived the war and reestablished Strikover Chassidus in Eretz Yisrael.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.yeshshem.com/hilulashevat.htm
