2 GIVN Nicha (Menucha) Nycha Nettie
2 SURN Weingold
2 _MARNM Goldblatt
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Elmont
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 SEP 1870
1 DEAT
2 DATE 11 APR 1954
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Memories of Channa Kleinerman Goldstein:  Nicha was a 'brent", a fiery personality, very strong-willed.  She and her husband lived in Coney Island when I came to the US, and she welcomed everyone who came over from
2 CONC  the old country and made sure we knew each other.  Whenever a Weingold relative was visiting NYC she would introduce us to each other.  This is how I met Lilly Lindall (Segal) and Shmuel Dovid Raichik.  
2 CONT
2 CONT We would go visit her and go to the beach.  Because it was a long trip from Williamsburg, I would sleep over at night so that I could enjoy a full day at the beach the next day.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicha had three children.  Sara Pessa never left Poland, and was killed along with her family in the Holocaust.  Yechil Wolf Goldblat tried to emigrate to the US but was rejected due to medical reasons, possibly intellectual disab
2 CONC ility, and he, too, was killed.  Irving emigrated successfully and married, but his marriage ended in a bitter divorce, and his children became estranged from him and from Nicha.  She would hang around the courtyards of their scho
2 CONC ol in the hope of seeing them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Up until WWII, she would try to send money back to her children in Poland.  During the tourist season, she rented out their bedroom and she and her husband slept on the porch.
