1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Khaia ליטמאנאוויץ nee Zilberberg was born to Avraham and Shifra. She was married to Mendl. Prior to WWII she lived in Poland. Khaia was murdered in the Shoah.
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT G16.6 Chaya Keila, born about 1925, married R. Menachem Mendel Meir Litmanowitz of Warsaw, wrote novellae to his father-in-law's volume of responsa, dated Purim 1939. He was a descendant of R. Solomon Rabinowitz, Admur Radomsko, t
2 CONC he ''Tiferet Shlomo'' (see Volume Two, 221). A page of Testimony for them was posted in 2007 by Yitzchak Shapiro in New York
2 CONT
2 CONT Source
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (3rd Edition) Volume 4, Chapter 12, page 421
2 CONT
2 CONT Please note: Menachem Mendel Meir Litmanowitz was a descendant of R. Solomon Rabinowitz, Admur Radomsko, and the Litmanowitz's who descend from R. Solomon Rabinowitz are descendants of his daughter Ruchla/Rachel who married Elieze
2 CONC r Lipman Litmanowitz. Based on generational considerations, we can deduce that Menachem Mendel Meir Litmanowitz must have been either a son or a grandson of one of Eliezer and Ruchla's sons.
