2 NOTE The family emigrated from Germany to Poland on the mistaken belief that since Shamo was a Polish citizen it would be easier to emigrate to Israel from there.  The baby in this picture died of diphteria in Poland.  They had another
3 CONC  baby and fled the Nazi invasion by moving toward Siberia, and later the Caucausus mountains.  The second baby died in Russia.  They were last heard from around 1943, and both were reportedly sick.  In one of her last letters to h
3 CONC er sister Erna, Sarah wrote, "I have no tears left to cry".
