1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Yitzkhak Rabinovitz was born in Radomsko to Tzvi and Ester. He was a rabbi and married to Roiza nee Bornshtein. Prior to WWII he lived in Plawno, Poland. Yitzkhak perished in Plawno, Poland at the age of 55.
2 CONT
2 CONT Was the author of ''Ohel Shlomo'', published in Piotrkow, 1924, containing the novellae of his grandfather, R. Solomon; ''Siach Yitchak'' (in ''Beit Shlomo''), published Piotrkow, 1927; ''Da'at Mordecai'', published by his son in 
2 CONC Keidaniai, 1939; and ''Ateret Shlomo'', published in Piotrkow, 1926.
