1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rabbi Samuel David Raichik (1905–1998) was a devoted emissary of the Chabad-Lubavitch movement and a pillar of Jewish education and outreach. Born in Poland, Rabbi Raichik displayed a love for Torah study and becam
2 CONC e deeply involved in the Chabad community at a young age. He studied at leading yeshivas, including Tomchei Temimim. He became a trusted disciple of the sixth Lubavitcher Rebbe, Rabbi Yosef Yitzchak Schneersohn, and later, the sev
2 CONC enth Rebbe, Rabbi Menachem Mendel Schneerson.
2 CONT
2 CONT During World War II, Rabbi Raichik risked his life to assist Jewish refugees, helping them escape persecution and rebuild their lives. After the war, he played a critical role in reestablishing Jewish institutions in European disp
2 CONC laced communities. In 1949, he was appointed by the Lubavitcher Rebbe to serve as a shliach (emissary) in Los Angeles, California, where Jewish life was in great need of revitalization.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Los Angeles, Rabbi Raichik founded schools, synagogues, and community programs that brought Torah education and Jewish traditions to thousands. He was instrumental in establishing the city as a vibrant center of Chabad activity
2 CONC . Known for his humility, warmth, and relentless dedication, Rabbi Raichik’s legacy continues to inspire Jewish outreach and education efforts worldwide.
