2 SURN Silverstein
2 NSFX of Beidozin
2 _MARNM Silverstein
1 NAME Abram Szmul Hersz //
2 GIVN Abram Szmul Hersz
2 SURN Zylbersztejn
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 27 NOV 1876
2 ADDR
3 CITY Radomsko
3 STAE Łódź Voivodeship
3 CTRY Poland
1 BURI
2 DATE SEP 1951
2 PLAC Scarborough, Ontario, Canada
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 SEP 1951
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Canada
1 OCCU Rabbi
1 TITL R'
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Tzvi" and "Hersh" are the same name meaning "stag" as in deer. One is Hebrew and the other is the same name in Yiddish. I BELIEVE he used Hersh as a nickname.
2 CONT
2 CONT  MY UNDERSTANDING is that our grandfather's name was Avraham Shmuel Tzvi (Hersh) Silverstein. His given name was Shmuel Tzvi. I understand that he took the name Avraham when he recovered from a very serious illness in his youth an
2 CONC d it was the custom to consider yourself reborn, so you take a new or additional name.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Victor Shields 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the  Zeida's  books is called Tiferes Shlomo. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Zeida asks about his son-in-law the Rov of Wierwzbenic, who I think was your (Jean Wagner's) grandfather, who took over the post of Rabbi when my grandfather left. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Radomsker Rabbi was often mentioned in the forwards of the Zeida's books as our ancestor and a source of some of our "Yeechus".
2 CONT
2 CONT The son to whom he is so complimentary to, in the second last paragraph, is Alter, Evelyn's father
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Toronto  1941
2 CONT
2 CONT To my dear friend whom I’ve known from youth, a native of my of my hometown, the wonderful scholar, intelligent and wise, renowned with praise, very prominent, our master Rav Feivish Jacabovitch  , may his light shine forth, of th
2 CONC e Bronx.
2 CONT
2 CONT My beloved, endeared to my soul, fellow native of my city , Reb Faivish, I rejoiced greatly to hear from my son, the upright and learned ……(missing some words) that you gave him an aliyah to the Sefer Torah and in calling his name
2 CONC  your honour immediately recognized that he is my son, and this is testimony that your honour has a good memory with my name etched in his good memory immediately identifying him as my son. 
2 CONT
2 CONT My Friend!  I rejoiced greatly that you are in New York and merited to escape from Bendin that is presently under the hands of the malicious, the brutish, the insane, the murderers, the Nazis, may their name and remembrance be obl
2 CONC iterated.  Who knows if they have not destroyed the city of our youth, the dear city of Bendin that was one the outstanding cities of Poland famous for it’s philanthropy and bursting with scholars of Torah, pious ones (Chasidim) a
2 CONC dored, superior and endeared.  Woe!  Where are the Chasidim and the community leaders? Where are the dear baalai batim, the philanthropists who gave generously to the impoverished?  Where are my acquaintances and my beloved, my br
2 CONC others and friends?  Where is my brother-in-law Fishel Pachter , where is my brother-in-law Lipa, where is my brother Paltiel from Sosnowice?  Where is the Rebbe of Sosnowice ?  Where are the tzadikim and rabbonim of Alexsander an
2 CONC d Krimilev : them and their children and families?  Where is my son-in-law the Rov of Wierwzbenic  may his light shine forth, a descendant of the Yid HaKodesh, and his daughters?  Woe! Woe! What can we say and what can we verbaliz
2 CONC e?   May the Almight-y have mercy on His nation and avenge the spilt blood of his servants and respond with vengeance to His enemies.  May we merit to both physical and spiritual redemption and ascend Zion with celebration.
2 CONT
2 CONT My dear Reb Faivish, may his light shine forth, please write me with a concise report of your history.  When you reached these shores.  Where you came from - if you came directly from Bendin or another city.  Who your uncle Gutenb
2 CONC erg from Zichov is.   Clarify everything and you will make me happy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please, please assist my son, may his light shine forth, in regards to the sefarim, and aside from that to befriend him and encourage him in the battle of Torah study, for he is intelligent and knowledgeable, a master of language 
2 CONC and grammar and an accomplished scholar (lamdon) complete with good traits and it is a pleasure to speak with him.  And I am not exaggerating because the facts can easily be verified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I remain his firm friend who seeks his welfare with love and joy and offers blessings of a Kesiva v’Chasima Tova
2 CONT
2 CONT From the soul of his firm friend HoRav Silverstein
2 CONT
2 CONT
