2 CONT
2 CONT The Jewish Chronicle - May 10 1996
2 CONT
2 CONT Southgate death
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Raphael Cymberg, emeritus minister of the Cockfosters and North Southgate Synagogue, died on Monday, aged 74.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Warsaw, Rabbi Cymberg was minister of the Notting Hill Synagogue before joining Cockfosters in 1958. He remained there until his retirement in 1986.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary next week
2 CONT
2 CONT The Jewish Chronicle - May 17 1996
2 CONT
2 CONT CYMBERG. Rabbi Raphael Wolf. We mourn the sudden passing of our dear cousin. He will be sadly missed by Anne, Howard, Laura and Darren Konskier.
2 CONT
2 CONT CYMBERG. Rabbi Raphael. Passed away suddenly on May 6, Greatly mourned and sadly missed. He will always be remembered by sister-in-law Fay (Phillips), brother-in-law Len, David, Judith; Ruth and his great-nephews Joshua, Alexander
2 CONC  and Ethan.
2 CONT
