2 NOTE leora, you have a clip from your parents wedding? 
3 CONT can you post it here?
3 CONT it is 100 % not my grandmother zipora perl, like reb shlomo said
3 CONT maybe the first wife
3 CONT
3 CONT rifka
3 CONT did you read my answer where the dark skin came from?
3 CONT it is very interesting, my brother the tolner rebbe, is dark and his firat name is yizchack
2 NOTE I still stand by my statement that the woman in the picture is the wife of the man in the picture, who is beyond doubt fetter Yitzchak Isaac z"l. Also that it is not the mime perl, there is not even the slightest resemblence.
3 CONT The only other thing thing that occured to me was perhaps the picture is of the fetter's first wife, Rivka Reisel. When I added
3 CONT the name to the picture I was unaware of his first wife so perhaps I was the culprit.
2 NOTE I have just returned from Ottawa, where we showed my uncle, Rabbi Allan Langner, all these pictures. He said with absolute certainty that this was Mima Perl (z"l), whom he knew well, and was not Deena (z"l). The few pictures of De
3 CONC ena that I have seen (including the film we have of my parents' wedding, where she is shown dancing) show a much heavier woman, and she would not have worn such modern clothes (which Mima Perl did wear). But perhaps we will never 
3 CONC know for certain. To answer Rifka, the Feter  Yitzhak Isaac and Deena had no children. There was an earlier marriage of Feter Yitzhak Isaac to someone else that only lasted a few months (also no children).
2 NOTE And I'm still wondering about rav yitzchok Isaacs background....i don't think they had children.
2 NOTE i am sorry to correct Rabbi Alan Langner. The person is definitely not my aunt perl but the wife of fetter yitsach isaac z"l.
2 NOTE According to Rabbi Allan Langner, the woman is Perl Langner (Twersky), not Deena.  
2 NOTE i think that the mother rifka (your named after her) was darkish [shloimee]
2 NOTE What is the origin of Rav Langner looking so dark, almost Sephardic? 
