2 CONT
2 CONT The Admor of Radzin, zt"l
2 CONT
2 CONT by S. Bruchi
2 CONT
2 CONT The Admor of Radzin, HaRav Avrohom Yissochor Englard zt"l, one of the elder admorim from Poland, was laid to rest on the fifth day of Chol Hamoed Succos at the age of 100.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Krimlov, Poland to HaRav Yeshayohu Hy"d, a descendent of the author of the Shach and Chosen Yeshuos who served as ravad in the city of Sossnovtza, and to his mother Esther Frummet o"h, the daughter of the Admor of Krimlov,
2 CONC  HaRav Nosson Nochum HaKohen Rabinowitz, the son of the Tiferes Shlomo of Radomsk.
2 CONT
2 CONT He acquired his early Torah learning from his uncle HaRav Dovid Moshe Rabinowitz, and HaRav Shmuel Aharon Pardes known as the Illui of Stashov.
2 CONT
2 CONT As the oldest grandson of the Admor of Krimlov he enjoyed a close relationship with his illustrious grandfather, in whose court he met most of the admorim of pre-Holocaust Poland.
2 CONT
2 CONT When he came of age, R' Avrohom Yissochor was chosen to become the son-in-law of the Admor of Radzin, the author of Tiferes Yosef, and he moved to Radzin. Following his father-in-law's petiroh the mantle of leadership was passed o
2 CONC nto his son, HaRav Shmuel Shlomo Hy"d. His brother-in-law, R' Avrohom Yissochor, assisted him in every matter and laid the foundations for the Sod Yeshorim yeshivos in Radzin and nearby towns and served as the nossi of the yeshivo
2 CONC s.
2 CONT
2 CONT When World War II broke out, he joined his brother-in-law the Admor, when he moved into the Vlodava Ghetto. There he attended to all matters of Judaism and devoted himself to helping Jews in crisis. When the Admor heard that Jews 
2 CONC were being killed in the forests of Sobibor he decreed a taanis of three days and three nights.
2 CONT
2 CONT During this horrific period the Nazis captured the bunker where the Admor and his family were staying and ordered all those inside to leave. They were then shot immediately. R' Avrohom Yissochor stayed inside, refusing to turn him
2 CONC self over to reshoim. They threw grenades into the bunker but miraculously the explosions left him unscathed. On 27 Iyar 5702 (1942) his brother-in-law, the Admor, was executed and died sanctifying the Name of Heaven on Shabbos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on the Admor's directives before his passing, R' Avrohom Yissochor of Vlodava, together with R' Motel Reichman the Pious whose wife Hy"d had also already been murdered, fled into the forests of Poland, where they remained in
2 CONC  hiding for almost two years. They wore the same set of clothes throughout this period, surviving under extreme conditions. But their lives were spared through Chasdei Shomayim.
2 CONT
2 CONT Throughout their period in hiding they kept all of the mitzvos, down to the smallest detail. Under the most adverse conditions they dug a hole in the ground and covered the pit with branches to fulfill the mitzvah of dwelling in a
2 CONC  succah. When Pesach arrived they managed to bake matzoh in the forest. Until his last day he kept in his possession a piece of the Afikoman he ate during his Seder Pesach in the forest. During this period of hiding he even arrang
2 CONC ed kiddushin for other Jews hiding from the Nazis and their accomplices.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the war ended and the extent of the destruction became known, based on vain hopes of finding the manuscripts left behind by the admorim of Radzin, he found that all of Jewish Radzin had been totally razed. He began wandering 
2 CONC through the cities of Poland, at first in the areas of Warsaw and Lodz. Although a forlorn refugee himself he helped other Jews rebuild their lives. He dedicated himself to resuscitating the spirit of Judaism, setting up Torah and
2 CONC  chessed institutions and arranging kiddushin for Jews who had lost all, but revealed great inner strength by starting Jewish homes from scratch.
2 CONT
2 CONT Later he returned to Sossnovtza where he assumed the post of rov and av beis din previously occupied by his father Hy"d. The town had become a transit point for thousands of refugees returning from exile in Russia and Siberia to v
2 CONC arious parts of Poland. His home drew all those in need of succor or assistance. He shared his bread and made his home available to refugees, attending to all of their needs in gashmiyus and ruchniyus. He provided a haven and an a
2 CONC ttentive ear for thousands of Jews passing through, including former admorim and rabbonim as well as the family of the Admor of Biale, the author of Chelkas Yehoshua.
2 CONT
2 CONT He attended to all of these matters in addition to a wealth of spiritual endeavors. In Sossnovtza he set up a talmud Torah and a yeshiva for refugees and their children. He organized shechitoh and set up a special beis din to rele
2 CONC ase agunos. He spent all of his personal funds to buy back sifrei kodesh in the hands of goyim.
2 CONT
2 CONT During this period he also served alongside HaRav Yitzchok Eizik Libes and others as a member of Rabbinical Committee of Postwar Polish Communities, a committee in operation for several years. He continued his activities in Sossno
2 CONC vtza for nearly three years, from 5705 (1945) to 5708 (1948).
2 CONT
2 CONT At the end of 5708, when almost no Jews remained in the Sossnovtza area, he traveled to Yanoville, a town outside of Paris where numerous Jewish refugees from Poland were gathered. Based on an invitation by friends from the Sossno
2 CONC vtza kehilloh who had settled in the US, he traveled to the US and stayed as their guest until 5712 (1952). In the US he strove to disseminate the works of his forefathers and rabbonim from Radomsk, such as Tiferes Shlomo and othe
2 CONC r seforim.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 5712 he agreed to requests from Radziner Chassidim gathered in Eretz Yisroel to join them. In Eretz Yisroel he build a new home with the Rebbetzin tlct"a, who played an important role in resurrecting the Radzin community.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 5713 (1953) a ceremony was held to install him as the Admor of Radzin. He then proceeded to build homes of Chassidim from the Radzin kehilloh in central cities throughout Eretz Yisroel and worked to rebuild Yeshivas Sod Yeshori
2 CONC m in Jerusalem.
2 CONT
2 CONT For decades he was heavily involved in the matter of techeiles for tzitzis based on the path laid down by his grandfather, the Admor of Radzin, HaRav Gershon Chanoch, the author of Orchos Chaim and Sidrei Taharos. The handling of 
2 CONC techeiles was discontinued under tragic circumstances during the Holocaust. He worked hard to renew the dye production process using the blood of a snail that is black in its original form.
2 CONT
2 CONT Circumstances required him to move to the US for several years. There, former members of the Sossnovtza kehilloh built him a beis medrash and a kehilloh of hundreds of Jewish survivors from Poland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Toward the end of 5731 (1971) he returned to Eretz Yisroel, settling in Bnei Brak where the large Radzin beis medrash was built. He set up a kollel there headed by HaRav Moshe Horowitz.
2 CONT
2 CONT He made himself available at all times to Jews of all backgrounds. Rich and poor, talmidei chachomim and distinguished figures along with simple Jews found an attentive listener in him. He received every Jew warmly and graciously.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notable for his ahavas Yisroel, good-heartedness and noble conduct he felt others' pain keenly and worked hard to assist those in need. A man of truth he often overlooked his own honor, displaying extraordinary humility.
2 CONT
2 CONT He spent the last six years confined to a hospital bed at Ma'ayanei Hayeshua in Bnei Brak. Jews around the world prayed for his recovery. His condition improved somewhat, but he remained bedridden and on the fifth day of Chol Hamo
2 CONC ed Succos he returned his pure soul to his Maker.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thousands took part in the levaya, which set out from the beis medrash on Rechov Aharonson in Bnei Brak, proceeding along Rechov Yerushalayim and Rechov R' Akiva. Gedolei Torah, roshei yeshivos, admorim and dayonim could be seen a
2 CONC ccompanying the mittoh.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Jerusalem the procession began at the Radzin center in the Yeshivas Chayei Olom building at Kikar HaShabbos, continuing via the Gur beis medrash, where a large crowd led by the Admor of Gur was waiting.
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased was then brought to Har Hamenuchos where he was buried in the rabbinical section.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Admor is survived by his wife, who stood by her great husband faithfully and devotedly, especially during his illness; his three sons, Rav Yeshayohu of Brooklyn, Rav Yitzchok and HaRav Shlomo, the rov of the Radzin beis medras
2 CONC h in Bnei Brak; and grandchildren and great- grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT רבי אברהם ישכר אנגלרד (ה'תרס"ט (?) - כ' בתשרי ה'תשס"ו) מראדזין היה האדמו"ר הששי בשושלת חסידות איזביצה ראדזין. נולד בשנת ה'תרס"ט (תאריך משוער) לרבי ישעיהו אנגלרד, רבה של העיר סוסנובצה בפולין, שהיה חתנו של האדמו"ר נתן נחום הכהן מקרי
2 CONC מילוב, בנו של האדמו"ר מראדומסק בעל החסד לאברהם. בבחרותו בחר בו האדמו"ר מרדכי יוסף אלעזר ליינר מראדזין, בעל התפארת יוסף, כחתן לבתו. עם פטירת חותנו בשנת ה'תרפ"ט נתמנה גיסו האדמו"ר שמואל שלמה ליינר מראדזין לאדמו"ר החמישי בחסידות ראדז
2 CONC ין ובשנים האלו שימש רבי אברהם ישכר כיד ימינו, ונתמנה על ידו לעמוד בראש ישיבת סוד ישרים בראדזין. בשליחות גיסו פתח עוד כשבעה סניפים בעיירות שונות בפולין, ודאג לניהולם הרוחני. במהלך השואה, בכ"ט באייר ה'תש"ב (1942) נהרג גיסו האדמו"ר ה
2 CONC חמישי בעיר וולאדובה בפולין. רבי אברהם ישכר ברח ליערות והצטרף לפרטיזנים, יחד עם עוד כמה מחסידי ראדזין. רבי אברהם ישכר שרד את השואה ונותר בין הצאצאים היחידים של רבי מרדכי יוסף אלעזר ליינר מראדזין. לאחר השואה חזר לעירו של אביו וכיהן 
2 CONC ברבנות בסוסנובצה במשך כמה שנים. בשנים אלו דאג לאוכל וללינה עבור אלפי פליטים. לאחר מספר שנים עבר האדמו"ר לשכונת קראון הייטס שבברוקלין, ובית מדרשו נודע כבית מדרשו של הרב מסוסנובצא. בלחץ חסידי ראדזין עלה לישראל והוכתר לאדמו"ר מראדזין
2 CONC  בכ"ט באייר ה'תשי"ג, בהיכל שלמה בתל אביב. בראשית כהונתו קבע את מקום מושבו בשכונת בית וגן בירושלים. לימים חזר לקהילתו בקראון הייטס. בסוף שנת תשל"א עלה שוב לארץ והתגורר במרכז החסידות החדש שנבנה ברחוב הרב אהרונסון בבני ברק. בבניין יש
2 CONC נם בתי מדרש, כוללים, מכון להוצאת ספרי איזביצא-ראדזין ומרכז לצביעת התכלת. תחת נשיאותו נוסדו שטיבלך של חסידי ראדזין בירושלים, בני ברק, חיפה, חולון, נתניה ופתח תקוה. בתל אביב יסד עוד שני שטיבלך, בנוסף על השטיבל שנוסד לפני השואה. בחלק
2 CONC  מהשטיבלך נפתחו כוללים. בירושלים הקים את ישיבת סוד ישרים ובבני ברק את ישיבת עטרת שלמה וישיבת תפארת יוסף. השקיע עמל בחידוש מצוות התכלת בציצית, על פי שיטתו של האדמו"ר השלישי, רבי גרשון חנוך הניך ליינר מראדזין. במהלך השואה פסקה מסורת
2 CONC  אופן הצביעה ולאחר שנים חודשה המלאכה תחת פיקוחו. בראש המרכז לצביעת התכלת העמיד את בנו, הרב יצחק אנגלרד. נפטר בכ' בתשרי, חול המועד סוכות ה'תשס"ו. משפחתו: בנו הרב ישעיהו אנגלרד (ארצות הברית). בנו הרב יצחק אנגלרד בבני ברק. בנו האדמו"
2 CONC ר שלמה יוסף אנגלרד, מכהן כאדמו"ר בבית מדרשו של אביו. נכדו הבכור הרב נתן נחום אנגלרד, מכהן כרב בית המדרש חסידי ראדזין בירושלים.
2 CONT
2 CONT (ויקיפדיה)
2 CONT
2 CONT HOLOCAUST TESTIMONIES
2 CONT
2 CONT Deponent: Orbach Pinkus
2 CONT
2 CONT Date of Birth: November 8, 1912
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth Place: Sosnowiec
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Symcha Binem and Maia (maiden name: Londner)
2 CONT
2 CONT Present Residence: Sosnowiec, ul. Wspolna 6A/3
2 CONT
2 CONT Profession: A member of presidium of the Jewish Committee in Sosnowiec
2 CONT
2 CONT At the turn of 1941/1942, a large Arbeitseinsatz took place in Sosnowiec. Moniek Meryn thought that the only way to save Jews from deportations is the voluntary departure of young people to work in Germany. Deportations in the reg
2 CONC ion had taken place already in 1940 when Jews were deported from Silesia to the Zaglebie and Chrzanow districts.
2 CONT
2 CONT There were also rumors that all Jews from our region annexed to Reich would be displaced to the Generale Gouvernement. Moniek Meryn wanted Jews to remain in the region of the Reich. He thought that going to work in Germany would h
2 CONC elp in this. but in general people didn’t want to go to work in Germany. This is why Meryn wanted to use the influence of orthodox spheres of life, most of all, the Rabbis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Meryn called a meeting of Rabbis in Sosnowiec at the beginning of 1941/1942. I don't remember exact date. At the meeting were present Rabbis: Jeszaja Englard, Szyja Gliksman and Dawid Halberntam from Sosnowiec, Hejnoch Dawid Frydb
2 CONC erg from Bedzin and the Rabbi from Grajewo who lived in Bedzin, the Rabbi from Dabrowa Gornicza and from Strzemieszyce. Meryn requested them to influence Jewish people by speeches in such a fashion that young people would go to wo
2 CONC rk in Germany.
2 CONT
2 CONT At this meeting, Rabbi Englard opposed Meryn's request. He said that it would be contradictory to Jewish ethics and to the rules of religion, to give part of society to save the rest. He said that let them {the Germans} capture by
2 CONC  themselves if there is no other choice. He referred to rules told by Majmonides.
2 CONT
2 CONT I know this all from a report by Lewin Heszek, who was close to Meryn. The meeting ended in a breakdown. After Englard's speech, there went other Rabbis who also didn’t yield this right to Meryn. I often went to the Community to f
2 CONC ind out what was the situation. My friends worked in the Community and, from through them, I knew about many secrets.
2 CONT
2 CONT I knew also that, from the beginning of the existance of the Jewish Community in Sosnowiec, by order of Meryn, work was done to preserve all documents related to the work of the Community and the fate of the Jews. Meryn brought fr
2 CONC om Dabrowa Gornicza one teacher, in particular - an historian, who wrote about incidents, official records of meetings, etc. I learned, also, that after certain difficult meetings in the matter of the Arbeitseinsatz, Meryn asked t
2 CONC he historian his opinion on this matter. The historian replied that the Meryn’s policy in this matter wasn’t good. Meryn was irritated and ordered the burning of all protocols (official records). I know about this from the same so
2 CONC urce, from Lewin.
2 CONT
2 CONT They say that Meryn sat and in silence waited until all will be burnt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pinkus Orbach
2 CONT
2 CONT Recorded by: mgr. Szternfinkiel N.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sosnowiec, October 18, 1947
2 CONT
2 CONT Corrected on November 19, 1947
2 CONT
