0 @N6000000006727748310@ NOTE This person and his descendants details are doubtful. The information is based on an interview of Boaz Zilbershatz with Shlomo Kaspari. Shlomo was about 90 years old at the day of the interview and all the details are from his mem
1 CONC ory. 
1 CONT This Hanoch Zilbershatz has a cousin whose family members got similar names, and the other one is more reliable since it is based on documents of the Polish researcher Petje.
1 CONT
1 CONT
0 @N6000000006727748642@ NOTE Learned Chemical Engineering in Belgium.
1 CONT Worked in France until World War II. 
1 CONT During the war was taken to Opola death camp and later on to Auchwits. Thanks to his chemical knowledge, was sent to work at the camp laundry and managed to survive. After two and a half years was released by the Russians. 
1 CONT After the war was nominated to manage a fuel factory in East Germany.  In 1949 went to visit his sister in Warsaw and then was arrested and accused as being a spy. Was released only after 18 months. 
1 CONT In 1958 immigrated to Israel and worked in the Hebrew University as a lecturer to Chemistry and a librarian. 
1 CONT Translated many science books to Hebrew. 
0 @N6000000006727748672@ NOTE Immigrated to Israel in 1934.
1 CONT Worked in the Dead Sea Industries until the Liberation war in 1948.
1 CONT Later on worked in the ministry of Agriculture and in TAHAL.
0 @N6000000006727748617@ NOTE Served as a Medical Doctor during the civil war in Spain and for the partizans during World War II. 
1 CONT Donated to the Botanic garden of the Hebrew University in Jerusalem.
0 @N6000000006727748502@ NOTE He came wth his father to Israel before the war, lived in Tel Aviv (11 Alenbi St.) then went back to Poland, and perished in the Holocaust.
0 @N6000000001173418973@ NOTE Shamir
